<title>USA: Elscint, GE Medical in joint venture.</title>
<headline>Elscint, GE Medical in joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elscint Ltd said it and GE Medical Systems, a unit of General Electric Co, signed a definitive agreement to form a 50-50 joint venture company to be located in Israel to engineer and manufacture nuclear medical imaging products for both partners.</p>
<p>The new venture will be named ELGEMS. Closing is expected within two months, subject to certain regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>The companies agreed in principle to form the joint venture on February 10.</p>
<p>Elscint is an advanced medical imaging company. GE Medical develops and produces diagnostic imaging equipment.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
